{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They know not neither do they understand</b> — the words of the poet, that he rebuked them yet they did not know and did not understand; or its meaning: they remained silent as though they did not know." "<b>They walk in darkness</b> — for a bribe blinds the eyes of the open-eyed." "<b>They are moved</b> — the foundations of the earth are worthy of being moved on account of the perversion of justice; or: the judges do not have pity [even though] all the foundations of the earth are moved."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 82, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:49.491133836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}